The Wind of the Wasteland:
Outside the city walls, the danger doesn't come only from the local wildlife. The wind, which may look like a simple sandstorm, causes partial paralysis of the human body.
Simply looking around becomes difficult; jumping becomes impossible, as does crouching. Moving your arms is not restricted.
You only need to breathe this air for two minutes to experience the negative effects described earlier. And that is already fatal.
The Hoyploma Health Department, in collaboration with local law enforcement, is actively working to prevent citizens from leaving the city without authorization and proper equipment.

Protecting Yourself from the Air:
High-ranking military personnel are equipped with full-body suits that shield them from the air in the Wasteland, preventing them from inhaling it. Two large air tanks are required to keep breathing.
Only military expedition personnel are authorized to wear these suits and leave the city.

The incidents:
Over the past few years, 56 residents have fled Hoyploma.
Not all of them have been found. The relevant authorities are currently taking additional measures to put an end to this.

What to do if you've “breathed in” the air:
If you're a fugitive who has breathed in the air and are having trouble moving, even if all seems lost, there are two ways to save yourself.
- Make yourself known to the expedition team, who will take you safely to the nearest hospital in your district. Specialized doctors will take care of you. The police in your district will handle the rest of the situation.
- Pressing the left and right arrow keys on the keyboard allows you to look around. Pressing M allows you to view or put away your map. As long as you’re outside, that’s all you can do.
Make your choice.



